+// EXO-BROKER: navigator.windowBroker, the shell's window broker API. Talks to
+// blink.mojom.WindowBroker, which the browser only binds for the shell
+// document; elsewhere the pipe closes and every call rejects.
+//
+// Push events: adding the first "windowadded" / "windowchanged" /
+// "windowremoved" / "windowfocusrequest" / "grantrevoked" listener subscribes
+// (WindowBroker.AddObserver). The snapshot that subscribing returns is
+// dispatched as one "windowadded" per existing window, then every later
+// change follows, so a page that listens before anything else builds its
+// whole window list from events. The observer is associated with the broker
+// pipe, so the snapshot can't race the events. Removing the last of those
+// listeners unsubscribes (the observer pipe closes); adding one again
+// subscribes again, with a new snapshot. Tabs, groups, shells and context
+// menus subscribe and unsubscribe the same way, each on their own events.
